Stop txiki.js standalone executables from creating ~/.tjs (T-792).

run-main creates TJS_HOME on every start, before it knows whether it is the
tjs CLI or a program compiled with `tjs compile`, and points lws' cookie jar
into it. todou's executables are the latter and use neither, so every todou
invocation would leave an empty ~/.tjs in the user's home, and every request
would write a cookies.txt there. This moves both to the two paths that do use
them: a TPK app and the tjs CLI itself. A standalone executable then has no
cookie jar at all, which is what lws does when none is configured.

Delete this patch, together with the run-main regeneration in .nix/txiki.nix
that exists only to carry it, once a txiki.js release stops creating TJS_HOME
and its cookie jar for bytecode standalone executables: compile a program that
fetches something with that release's `tjs compile`, run it with an empty HOME,
and check that HOME stays empty and the fetch does not stall.

--- a/src/js/run-main/index.js
+++ b/src/js/run-main/index.js
@@ -13,20 +13,26 @@
 
 
 /**
- * Before we do anything else, create our "home" directory,
- * so other parts of the code which need it can find it.
- * Also set the cookie jar path, since it's needed when
- * initializing lws.
+ * The "home" directory, and the cookie jar inside it, are set up only where
+ * they are used: TPK apps and the tjs CLI itself. A bytecode standalone
+ * executable is somebody else's program and must not leave ~/.tjs behind on
+ * every run. Nor may it have a jar path without the directory: lws locks the
+ * jar on every client request, and waits about five seconds for a lock file
+ * it cannot create before giving up. Without a path lws keeps no jar at all.
+ * lws reads the path once, when it is first used, and nothing before the two
+ * calls below uses it.
  */
 const TJS_HOME = getTjsHome();
 
-try {
-    mkdirSync(TJS_HOME, { recursive: true });
-} catch (_) {
-    // Ignore.
-}
+function ensureTjsHome() {
+    try {
+        mkdirSync(TJS_HOME, { recursive: true });
+    } catch (_) {
+        // Ignore.
+    }
 
-core.setCookieJarPath(path.join(TJS_HOME, 'cookies.txt'));
+    core.setCookieJarPath(path.join(TJS_HOME, 'cookies.txt'));
+}
 
